71   2025). All four compare two modes of the same checkpoint. OLMo 3 7B (OLMo Team, 2026) is
72   analyzed separately because it compares Think and Instruct checkpoints. Earlier Phi and Liquid ex-
73   periments remain secondary appendix results. In the audited Qwen3.5 template, the assistant sufﬁx
74   differs as follows:
                                   think          <|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n
75                                 no-think       <|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n
                                                  \n</think>\n\n

76   The shared preﬁx is intentional: in this Qwen3.5 template, no-think opens and immediately closes
77   an empty think block before the answer begins.
78   Qwen3-4B uses its documented soft switch instead.                       Both conditions keep
79   enable_thinking=True; the user message ends in /think or /no_think. The two prompts
80   then share the same assistant header, and both modes ﬁrst emit <think>. Their next-token
81   distributions sharply separate: thinking mode’s top token is the single-newline continuation that
82   begins nonempty reasoning, while no-think’s top token is the double-newline continuation of an
83   empty block. We therefore supply the same <think> token to both conditions and perform the
84   Qwen3 causal audit at that ﬁrst divergent decision. This is not the hard template switch obtained
85   with enable_thinking=False.

86   Prompt sets. Table 3 states exactly where prompts come from and how they are used. The ﬁxed
87   vector never sees an AIME prompt during ﬁtting or selection.

88   Terms used below. An activation is the vector of numbers passed between transformer layers. The
89   residual stream is this main layer-to-layer path. A donor is the run whose mode we copy; the target
90   is the run we modify. A tail patch of width 2 copies activations only at the ﬁnal two audited tokens.
91   A ﬁxed mode vector is one average activation difference learned on other prompts. Appendix G
92   gives intuitive and mathematical deﬁnitions together.

