125   We ﬁt an uncentered SVD basis to {∆i } on training prompts, then patch only the projection of
126   each held-out prompt’s exact donor-target difference into the learned subspace. This is a subspace-
127   sufﬁciency test: at evaluation time, the held-out exact difference supplies the coordinates inside a
128   basis learned only from training prompts. It therefore tests whether the causal mode information lies
129   in a shared low-dimensional subspace, not whether a single ﬁxed steering vector fully determines
130   the branch.

