454   F.3 Nemotron generation details

455   Ten-seed entry-format audit. We ﬁrst test the opening under ten paired generation/random-vector
456   seed settings, using the same 30 frozen non-math prompts and the same frozen width-2 controller.
457   Each run changes exactly the ﬁrst generated decision and is capped at 64 tokens. We pre-specify
458   an exact <think> opening as the forward generated-format endpoint. The ﬁxed vector reaches that
459   endpoint on 293/300 generations, versus 0/300 for the norm-matched random vectors. The paired
460   difference is .977. A two-way bootstrap that resamples both prompts and paired run settings gives
461   a 95% interval of [.930, 1.000] from 10,000 resamples. Every individual run scores between 27/30
462   and 30/30 for the ﬁxed vector, while every random-vector run scores 0/30.

