463   All 300 ﬁxed off-to-think interventions select <th as the ﬁrst token. The seven strict opening
464   failures occur during ordinary sampling after that intervened token and produce malformed con-
465   tinuations such as <think offhand or <think off-topic>; they remain counted as failures.
466   They are concentrated on three prompt values: multiturn_02 twice, nonenglish_02 once, and
467   nonenglish_04 four times. We omit a reverse generated-format rate because merely failing to open

                                                                       15
468   with <think> does not distinguish a clean direct answer from an unrelated or malformed random-
469   vector output. We instead report the saved ﬁrst-step donor-win endpoint in both directions. For
470   each prompt, the ﬁxed ﬁrst-step distribution is deterministic and therefore repeats across the ten run
471   settings; the 300/300 ﬁxed rows in each direction are descriptive, not 300 independent distributional
472   replications. The random-vector controls vary across runs. Reverse ﬁxed generation is also greedy,
473   so its output repeats across seeds. The 64-token cap makes this an entry-format audit; the separate
474   experiment below supplies the 1,024-token completion, length, and repetition evidence.

475   F.4 AIME 2026 answer quality after a frozen entry intervention

476   This experiment asks the reviewer’s downstream question directly: what answer quality follows after
477   the recovered thinking branch is entered? The controller is the previously frozen Nemotron off-to-
478   thinking vector: width 2, boundary 28, and α = 4, ﬁtted and selected only on the 30 GSM8K and
479   30 numeric MATH-500 prompts. It uses all 30 AIME 2026 problems, one paired seed (20260728),
480   four conditions, and one equal budget without retries. The controller, tasks, prompts, conditions,
481   samplers, seeds, grading, and uncertainty procedure were ﬁxed before the ﬁrst AIME 2026 genera-
482   tion. After inspecting the initial 8,192-token run and ﬁnding that 65/120 rows were truncated, we
483   committed a corrective protocol and reran all 120 generations from scratch at the 32,768-token set-
484   ting in NVIDIA’s model-card example (NVIDIA, 2025). This longer run is the primary analysis;
485   the initial run remains separate as superseded resource-bounded provenance. The correction was
486   speciﬁed before any 32,768-token generation, but it was post-hoc to the 8,192-token result and is
487   not a preregistration. An earlier AIME 2025 timing pilot is excluded from every result.
488   Canonical off generation is greedy; the other three conditions use the protocol’s thinking sampler.
489   For the ﬁxed and norm-matched random conditions, the intervention changes only the ﬁrst next-
490   token distribution. The sampled token is appended to the untouched off-mode prompt, the patched
491   state is discarded, and the model generates every later token normally. The primary score requires
492   the response to stop before the cap and its last syntactically valid \boxed{N} integer to match the
493   gold answer. A ﬁnal standalone-integer parser is secondary. Table 15 reports every condition; no
494   entry, completion, cap, or repetition failure is removed.

