495   The ﬁxed vector produces the exact <think> opening, the thinking donor’s top-1 entry token, a
496   donor win, and effective control on all 30 problems. Its successful-entry subset is therefore the full
497   ﬁxed-condition population, and every conditional comparison is identical to the unconditional one.
498   Fixed is 15–0 against off and 14–0 against random, which uses the same thinking sampler, while
499   its 4–3 comparison with canonical thinking is not signiﬁcant. Fixed also completes more often than
500   thinking, 26/30 versus 23/30.
501   The hash-bound manual audit covers all 120 traces. All 34 strict positives have supported ﬁnal an-
502   swers and no false positive. The 25 cap hits contain two incidental or intermediate gold-number
503   occurrences and 23 with no gold occurrence; none contains a supported or later-retracted gold an-
504   swer. All 32 boxed/ﬁnal-integer disagreements are faithful, with no parser false positive or false

                                                                16
505   negative. All 36 ﬁxed/reference strict discordances reﬂect answer quality (33 ﬁxed wins and three
506   losses), not termination or parsing. One supported ﬁxed answer, task 22’s 754, triggers the conserva-
507   tive tail-repetition heuristic; manual review conﬁrms that its derivation and ﬁnal answer are coherent,
508   so the primary strict score retains it. Removing only the completion gate changes no score.
509   The cap-only rerun also provides a continuation check. All 55 rows that stopped at 8K are exactly
510   identical in text and token IDs, and all 65 old cap hits reproduce their exact 8,192-token and decoded-
511   text preﬁxes. By 32K, 21 of those rows stop correct, 19 stop wrong, and 25 remain capped; no
512   previously correct row regresses. Fixed tasks 3, 4, and 8 were capped at 8K and now ﬁnish with
513   supported correct boxes; task 3 had already emitted its correct box before the cap, while tasks 4 and
514   8 had not. In contrast, task 28 canonical thinking derives the correct candidate 107, then rejects it
515   and ﬁnishes with 139, illustrating why intermediate number mentions are not scored as answers.
516   An independent post-run script reconstructs the frozen prompts and vectors, veriﬁes recorded to-
517   ken IDs against decoded text, recomputes strict and secondary correctness, and regenerates every
518   aggregate, bootstrap interval, paired count, and McNemar test. It passes on all 120 unique prompt-
519   by-condition rows. The one-seed experiment establishes that a causally selected entry token can
520   change later answer quality in this paired run; its task bootstrap does not estimate sampling-seed
521   variation. The hash manifest, machine-readable report, exhaustive manual audit, and 8K-to-32K
522   comparison are included with the artifact.

523   One ﬁxed-vector step on 30 held-out non-math prompts. We use the frozen width-2 vector
524   learned from the 60 GSM8K/MATH-500 training prompts and apply it for exactly the ﬁrst generated
525   decision. We then let the model continue freely for up to 1,024 tokens. The evaluation set has
526   30 previously frozen prompts: six each from ﬁve non-mathematical categories. The experiment
527   contains exactly 180 generations: two canonical modes, two ﬁxed-vector directions, and two norm-
528   matched random-vector directions for every prompt.

